        "Content": "Leonard Wilson Keenan \r\n\r\nA Name To Remember \r\n\r\n3 Bedroom, 1 Bathroom , Mid Terrace Red Brick Home \r\nPerfect for renovation \r\nEarly viewing is advised \r\n\r\nRichard Todd and LWK Groupe are delighted to present 18 Clonmore Terrace to the Dublin 3 property market. \r\n\r\n18 Clonmore Terrace is a charming three-bedroom, one-bathroom red-brick mid-terrace family home, ideally located on a quiet cul-de-sac in Dublin 3. Full of character and charm, this lovely property offers well-proportioned accommodation throughout and enjoys a superb location close to the city centre and the Royal Canal.\r\nOn arrival at the property, you will immediately notice the signature Dublin red-brick façade, with steps leading up to the front door. Entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright and inviting hallway. To the left is the front living room, which features high ceilings and a beautiful feature fireplace, while the large window overlooks the front of the property and allows plenty of natural light into the room. Moving through the property, you will find the second family room, which also benefits from a feature fireplace and provides a versatile additional reception space. This room could also be utilised as another bedroom, depending on the new owners' needs.\r\n\r\nMoving further through the house, you arrive at the kitchen, which has an abundance of both base and eye-level storage, making it a practical and functional space for everyday family living. A window overlooks the rear garden, providing natural light, while there is also direct access from the kitchen into the back garden. The rear garden offers a pleasant outdoor space and benefits from double-door access to the rear laneway, providing convenient additional access.\r\n\r\nMoving upstairs, the master bedroom is positioned to the front of the property and features two windows and a feature fireplace. This is a bright and airy room with plenty of natural light. The second double bedroom is also a generous room and benefits from its own feature fireplace, while the large family bathroom completes this level.\r\n\r\nThe attic conversion is currently used as the third bedroom and built as storage. The space benefits from two Velux windows, allowing additional natural light into the room and creating a versatile area with excellent potential for a variety of uses, subject to any necessary planning requirements.\r\n\r\nThe location of 18 Clonmore Terrace is sure to appeal to those looking for the convenience of city living while still enjoying a quiet residential setting. The property is situated close to the Royal Canal, where the canal towpath provides an excellent amenity for walking, running and cycling. North Strand, Ballybough and the surrounding Dublin 3 area offer a wide selection of local shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities, while Dublin City Centre is within easy reach, making the property particularly attractive to commuters and those working in the city.\r\n\r\nThe property also benefits from excellent access to public transport, with a number of bus routes serving the surrounding area and providing convenient connections throughout Dublin. The IFSC, East Point Business Park and Dublin City Centre are all within easy reach, making this an ideal location for  and families alike. There is also a good selection of schools and educational facilities in the surrounding area, adding further appeal for those looking to establish a family home in this well-connected part of the city.\r\n\r\nCombining traditional Dublin red-brick character with generous and versatile accommodation, high ceilings, feature fireplaces, bright bedrooms, a converted attic and a rear garden with access to the back laneway, 18 Clonmore Terrace is a property that offers charm, convenience and excellent potential. Situated on a quiet cul-de-sac while remaining close to the Royal Canal and Dublin City Centre, this wonderful home is sure to prove popular when it comes to the market and viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate what this property has to offer.\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
